      "reviewer_reference": "Root supplied-form challenge and independent B source re-review,2026-11-08; source molecules are not sufficient proof of historical supplied reagent.",
      "withdrawal_reason": "MediaDB compound38 explicitly represents Zinc as BiGGzn2, CHEBI29105, Zn2+/Zn(II), and the two complete TAP recipes are expressed as ionic nutrient components. This establishes the source database nutrient concept, not a physically supplied isolated zinc ion, metallic zinc, zinc salt or chelate. Original Boyle/Morgan2009 culture methods state TAP for heterotrophic/mixotrophic growth and similar medium without acetic acid for autotrophy, citing Harris1989; the article section does not specify the zinc reagent. The prior Zn2+ owner draft did preserve this conceptual distinction, but it is withdrawn from actionable ingredient proposals because the historical supplied-form bridge remains unestablished. Retain all existing ionic source identifiers and both occurrences; do not reconstruct a salt from the nutrient count or generic TAP conventions."
